  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 240 AM MDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nPersistent cloud cover and light rain continue across the \nCentral Mountains this morning as the eastern edge of a Pacific \nNorthwest low channels moisture overhead. High-resolution \nconvective-allowing models (CAMs) indicate this activity will \nbriefly wane late this morning through the afternoon, offering a\nshort dry window. While isolated showers may redevelop late \ntonight across the Central Mountains, the rest of eastern Idaho \nwill remain dry. Afternoon maximum temperatures will reach the \nlower 80s across the lower Snake Plain and Magic Valley, with \nmountain zones holding in the mid-to-upper 70s.\n\nLow-level southerly flow will strengthen on Sunday ahead of the\napproaching upper-level low. Guidance continues to trend storm-\ntotal precipitation lower (0.10\" to 0.30\") while delaying rain \nchances until late Sunday evening and overnight. Consequently, \nthe vast majority of eastern Idaho will enjoy dry daylight hours\non Sunday, with valley temperatures warming back into the lower\n80s.\n\nEarly morning rain showers and cloud cover on Monday will clear\nout from west to east during the early-to-mid afternoon, with \nprecipitation ending well before sunset. This timing allows the \nsecond half of the holiday to remain usable for outdoor \nfestivities, albeit in a seasonably cool environment with highs \nin the 60s and lower 70s. Clearing skies Monday night will drive\novernight lows into the 30s across high country basins and 40s \nin valley floors.\n\nTuesday remains cool with lower-elevation highs in the lower-to-\nmid 70s and mountain highs in the 60s. Flow turns predominantly\nzonal Wednesday and Thursday, pushing valley temperatures back\ntoward seasonal averages in the upper 70s and lower 80s under\ngenerally dry conditions. Model guidance indicates another\nPacific Northwest trough digging south Friday into next weekend,\nwhich could lower temperatures slightly while increasing cloud\ncover and low-end precipitation chances.",
